WEBVTT

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:09.400
Yusei Fudo.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:10.900
Yusei Fudo!

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.130
Are you listening?

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:16.600
The authorities have seized 
your D-Wheel and deck.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:18.950
Yusei Fudo!

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:22.300
Satellite citizens trespassing into 
Neo Domino City

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.300
without permission is a heinous crime.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:30.090
Therefore, the Public Maintenance Department 
has rendered the following verdict:

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.360
One count!  You will be 
inscribed with a marker.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:44.500
Under Neo Domino City jurisdiction, 
this mark symbolizes incompatibility.

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:50.080
It means that you are not allowed 
to live in our jurisdiction!

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:20.620
No matter how far apart we 
are, we can't be stopped

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:25.610
That's deeply engraved into us

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:34.110
So don't be afraid of getting hurt

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:40.120
Break through even further

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:45.630
While carrying you beliefs in your heart

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:52.780
There's always only one truth

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:56.670
So feel the voice of your heart

00:01:57.870 --> 00:02:01.460
With your unwavering emotions

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.560
Seize the signs of tomorrow

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:42.920
Look at My Treasured Deck!

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:50.620
One count!  Yusei Fudo will take part in a 
reeducation program at a detention center for one month.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:51.890
Hurry up and get on!

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:59.180
This is to reconfirm that you know the laws of Neo 
Domino City.  Every violator must take this program.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:56.870
Pardon me.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:05.540
After finishing the program, 
you will spend six months

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:11.110
at the Neo Domino City expansion factory 
before being sent home to Satellite.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:12.350
Hey.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.680
Hey hey.

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:19.920
I heard you were caught 
trespassing.  Same here.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:22.030
My name is Yanagi.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:24.070
Nice to meet you.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:31.590
You were caught at Duel Stadium, 
right?  I was nearby at the time.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:35.730
It was incredible.  All the lights went out.

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:47.360
But what surprised me the 
most was that red dragon!

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:54.510
Weren't you inside the stadium at that time?

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:55.810
What do you know?

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:59.190
Bro, how did you bring that out?

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:04.950
Weren't you having a Riding Duel?  You 
can bring that dragon out during a duel?

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.750
How long have I been here?

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:33.970
Good morning.  Since this 
morning, Master Atlas.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:37.760
The Director himself brought you here.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:44.130
He thought the reason you were upset 
was because the duel wasn't completed.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:47.630
Wait!  How did you know that 
the duel wasn't completed?

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:52.230
I'm sorry.  I saw the whole thing.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:55.590
Master Atlas, where are you going?

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:58.450
Please wait, Master Atlas!

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:08.750
As you can see, when Red Dragon 
Archfiend and Stardust Dragon clashed,

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:12.750
the Moment's rotations increased rapidly.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:21.310
This supports the conditions required for 
resurrecting the ancient Crimson Dragon.

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:22.950
That's correct!

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:25.850
This event occurred just 
when we finalized plans

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:28.950
to include Moment in all 
parts of Neo Domino City!

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:33.980
This is great news!

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:39.450
This is when we lost power, 
so the recording stopped.

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:44.600
I see.  That means the Crimson 
Dragon hasn't been filmed clearly.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:45.760
Correct.

00:05:58.550 --> 00:05:59.620
This way!

00:06:04.570 --> 00:06:08.180
You're G2MA2-88.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:11.050
Starting today, you will be 
referred to by your number.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:17.760
Everyone who caused problems in the city 
are housed here to undergo reeducation.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:26.440
Other than trespassers like you, people 
unfit for society are also kept here.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:35.840
Stop!  This is your room!  Enter!

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:41.050
Hooray!  I can finally sleep in a bed.

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:43.920
The reeducation program 
starts in the afternoon.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:47.390
Until then, you should 
think about what you did.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:50.280
Hello.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:51.610
What do you want?

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:55.060
I want to throw a welcome 
party for the new arrivals.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:58.820
As an old-timer, I'll teach 
them the rules of this place.

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:02.810
Again?  Don't cause too much trouble.

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:12.010
This place is big.  And it's also new.

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:14.760
You haven't answered my question yet.

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:17.130
About what?

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:18.900
About the red dragon.

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:20.200
Bro.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:22.890
Did you bring a deck?

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:25.670
We'll talk afterwards.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:27.380
We're not allowed to bring one.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:31.510
Ta-daa!

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:38.980
After visiting various detention centers, 
I learned that you always need a deck.

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:40.770
You're allowed to duel here?

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:43.590
It's the same inside as outside. 
Even in a detention center,

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:46.590
there are ones who are in control 
and ones being controlled.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:49.600
Who's who is decided by a duel.

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:51.300
A duel.

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:56.890
Master Atlas!  Please wait, Master Atlas!

00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:06.520
This shows that when the King had them both 
out simultaneously, Moment didn't run amok!

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:08.750
But it did when they clashed.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:13.990
So did something happen when the two battled?

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:20.300
I'm sorry, Director.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.620
What is this?

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:26.780
Why are you watching this?

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:28.920
Please calm down.

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:31.670
This is the Public Maintenance Department.

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:34.880
We protect the peace in Neo Domino City.

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:38.640
It is our duty to learn about strange 
events that occur in the city.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:44.140
Information connected to the people 
of the stars is especially important.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.310
You know something.

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:51.000
When the Crimson Dragon appeared, 
I felt a pain on this mark!

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:57.100
That's right.  According to 
legend, you are a Signer.

00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:00.020
You're a person who has 
the mark of the dragon.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.020
Signer?

00:09:02.510 --> 00:09:06.190
You are the chosen one.  You 
are a person of the stars.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:09.430
However, Yusei also had the mark!

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:12.120
It was linked to my mark!

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:15.530
What?  That person from Satellite?

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.010
You didn't see it?

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:22.680
Unfortunately, the visuals were 
cut due to the power outage.

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:24.730
I saw it!

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:28.580
Yusei's arm also had the mark!

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:32.750
But he didn't have it two years ago!

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:36.480
Stop!  Pause the monitor!

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:37.780
Rewind!

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:40.040
Right here!

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:44.180
Enlarge that section.

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:45.880
Easily done.

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:49.760
This is…

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:52.660
Meteor Stream!

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:56.270
I see.  Meteor Stream.

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:59.660
King, what you activated right before was…

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:03.940
I activate a Speed Spell!  End of the Storm!

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:08.950
End of the Storm destroys 
all monsters on the field.

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:16.090
For every destroyed monster, the 
player takes 300 points of damage.

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:21.850
That's right!  That was a 
strategy to get Stardust back!

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:24.190
I'm counting on you, Stardust!

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:32.090
He takes damage, and then it was supposed 
to return to my field after he released it!

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:36.720
But at the very end, he was 
going to use Meteor Stream.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:43.260
When a released monster resurrects, 
that card deals 1000 points of damage.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:45.630
That means…

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:49.020
I had 900 life points.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:51.590
If I took 1000 points of damage...

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:53.500
Zero!

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:00.710
I lost to him!

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:02.500
I…

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:07.310
Don't worry about it.

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:10.030
No one knows what happened last night.

00:11:10.030 --> 00:11:15.870
But I know!  The King knows!  There's 
no way I can forget this duel!

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:17.580
Where is he?

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:19.460
Where is he right now?

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:25.680
It's regular policy to quarantine 
people who arrive from Satellite.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:28.080
He is no exception.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:30.770
He would be at the detention center by now.

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:38.670
I'm going to meet him.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:43.500
You can't.  Thank about 
your role as the King.

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:47.810
Don't you want to know about the 
people of the stars and Signers?

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:50.500
Don't you want to know who you truly are?

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:59.910
Welcome to my duel field.

00:12:24.270 --> 00:12:27.570
I'm Himuro.  This is my realm.

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:33.120
Since you're new, you don't know 
that there are two sets of rules.

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:36.220
One for inside the detention center 
and another for the outside.

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:37.230
Got it?

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.980
And I rule the inside.

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:43.110
I know who you are!

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:47.530
You're the pro duelist Jin Himuro, right?

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:49.240
Shut up, geezer!

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:54.040
Awesome!  I'm so lucky that I can 
meet you in a place like this!

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:58.820
Hey bro, I've seen him several times on TV.

00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:00.810
Stop talking about the past!

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:03.530
That geezer can't sense 
the tension in the air.

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:07.010
Talking about Himuro's past is not allowed.

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:10.280
Hey geezer! When I talk about 
the rules on the inside,

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:13.780
it means that you have to duel 
me to determine your rank.

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:18.380
The lower rank must obey the higher rank!

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:20.460
That's what I thought.

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:24.160
Since I thought this was going 
to happen, I brought a deck.

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:27.140
My deck is incredible.

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:31.420
It's the rarest of the rare!  
I call it the treasure deck!

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:35.450
Look!

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:36.660
Treasure deck?

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:38.600
The rarest of the rare?

00:13:39.530 --> 00:13:41.350
It's good that you're prepared.

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:43.260
How about you?

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:45.030
I don't have one.

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:49.210
You're a trespasser from Satellite.

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:52.320
That means you won't have a deck.

00:13:53.210 --> 00:13:56.510
Just by being a citizen of Satellite, 
you're the lowest of the low.

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:03.310
Well now, my bro didn't know anything.

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:06.030
Take it easy on me, Himuro-chan.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:07.940
Stop saying my name like that!

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:11.650
Let me borrow a Duel Disk.

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:17.980
I'm so happy that I can 
duel against Himuro-chan.

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:18.940
Geezer!

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:20.990
Be careful, Himuro.

00:14:20.990 --> 00:14:24.000
He said it's the rarest 
of the rare.  I'm worried.

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:28.220
He's just bragging.  I'll 
break through his disguise.

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:31.150
Oh really?  Am I bragging?

00:14:31.150 --> 00:14:33.320
Watch, bro.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:37.660
Grandpa, I'll let you go first.

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:41.650
Okay, let's duel!

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:48.480
My turn!

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:50.830
First, I'll show you this!

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:54.230
It's an incredible card 
that I acquired recently!

00:14:54.580 --> 00:15:00.110
This card was found deep in South America 
and depicts a strange ancient item!

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:03.580
Stop bragging and hurry 
up and play it, geezer.

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:09.170
Watch and be shocked!  I summon 
Crystal Skull in defense position!

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:17.010
Come out, Crystal Skull!

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:21.460
Why?

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:23.840
Don't you know that card's monster effect?

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:29.190
The player who summons Crystal 
Skull takes 1000 points of damage.

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:31.330
Oh no!

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:35.760
No wonder it's an ancient 
treasure.  There's a curse on it!

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:41.110
I can't believe you put such 
a useless card in your deck.

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:42.590
Oh yeah!

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:50.230
There's a rumor that Crystal Skull's elaborate 
design could only be created using modern methods.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:53.990
That means it's a forgery.

00:15:53.990 --> 00:15:55.350
That's not true!

00:15:55.350 --> 00:16:01.100
Ancient people created Crystal Skull using 
techniques that even we don't know about!

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:03.160
That's enough!  It's the 
end of your turn, right?

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:04.660
Yeah.

00:16:04.660 --> 00:16:06.540
Then it's my turn!

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:10.850
I activate the spell card Cost Down!

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:16.180
Until the End Phase, the Level of 
all monsters is decreased by two!

00:16:17.800 --> 00:16:19.330
Lower the Level?

00:16:19.650 --> 00:16:24.220
All I did was make my skill level 
in dueling match yours, grandpa.

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:28.940
I discard one card in my hand 
and summon Level 6 Ushi Oni!

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:35.820
Ushi Oni!

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:41.260
He said that he would lower his skill level, 
but he brought out Ushi Oni.  Himuro is cruel.

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:47.550
Due to Cost Down, Level 6 
Ushi Oni becomes Level 4,

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:51.300
so I can summon it without 
releasing another monster.

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:54.230
Ushi Oni, attack Crystal Skull!

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:59.060
No!  Don't destroy my Crystal Skull!

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:08.930
My Crystal Skull!

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:13.990
It's fate that fakes quickly 
vanish.  It's your turn, grandpa.

00:17:14.650 --> 00:17:15.670
Bring it.

00:17:15.670 --> 00:17:18.420
It's time for my next card.

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:20.300
I draw!

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:23.940
This is pretty good too.

00:17:24.900 --> 00:17:31.180
Its defense points are excellent!  Look at 
this card.  I summon it in defense position!

00:17:39.310 --> 00:17:40.150
Awesome!

00:17:40.150 --> 00:17:42.290
I've never seen a card like this!

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:44.690
That's Ashoka Pillar.

00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:50.190
That's right.  Ashoka Pillar is a mysterious 
iron pole that exists in India.

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:56.000
This perfect iron pole was made using 
techniques that didn't exist during that era!

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:59.650
Grandpa, do you really want to duel?

00:17:59.650 --> 00:18:02.890
You've played nothing but lame cards!

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:05.410
Are you making fun of me?

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:08.240
I'll show you even more shocking cards!

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:13.740
From my hand, I equip the spell 
card Spirit Mask on Ashoka Pillar!

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:20.310
So?  What are you planning to do with that?

00:18:21.230 --> 00:18:23.750
Stay tuned.

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:25.570
I end my turn.

00:18:25.570 --> 00:18:27.800
My turn.  I draw!

00:18:27.800 --> 00:18:32.430
Grandpa, all you want to 
do is show off your cards.

00:18:32.430 --> 00:18:35.290
All your cards are useless garbage 
that don't work well together!

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:41.430
This is a waste of time!  I'll 
wipe away those garbage cards!

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:44.000
First, I release Ushi Oni!

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:45.450
Why?

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:48.110
I Special Summon Giant Ushi Oni!

00:18:48.630 --> 00:18:50.310
This is...

00:18:53.260 --> 00:18:58.380
Giant Ushi Oni is a monster that can 
only be summoned by releasing Ushi Oni.

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:04.690
Giant Ushi Oni, attack Ashoka 
Pillar!  Specter's Bite!

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:10.040
Well done, Himuro!

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:19.450
You're pathetic.  But don't 
think you've escaped yet!

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:25.840
When Ashoka Pillar is destroyed, 
you take 2000 points of damage!

00:19:28.190 --> 00:19:31.340
And don't forget the effect of Spirit Mask.

00:19:31.340 --> 00:19:34.150
When that card is sent to the graveyard,

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:37.650
you have \to send another card 
in your hand to the graveyard.

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:39.640
Oh yeah.

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:46.410
It takes skill to gather 
that many useless cards.

00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:50.520
Giant Ushi Oni's monster effect!

00:19:50.520 --> 00:19:56.450
If it destroys your monster in 
battle, it can attack again!

00:19:57.640 --> 00:20:00.100
Attack grandpa directly!

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:09.680
Are you okay, grandpa?

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:13.820
Grandpa, you lose.

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:15.580
Sheesh.

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:22.520
Not only didn't I lose any life points, but 
you dueled in a manner that was insulting to me!

00:20:24.090 --> 00:20:27.960
Grandpa, I give you the lowest rank possible!

00:20:29.470 --> 00:20:31.470
I wasn't insulting you.

00:20:31.470 --> 00:20:36.700
I just wanted to show these cards 
to an incredible duelist like you!

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:41.770
I love these cards!  Am I 
not allowed to love them?

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:47.030
It's true that I don't know 
much about effects and such.

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:54.610
But I love these cards because they tell 
me about the mysteries of the human world.

00:20:54.630 --> 00:21:00.050
Please move your foot.  My 
precious cards are in pain!

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:03.030
How horrible!

00:21:10.900 --> 00:21:12.930
What are you doing, you punk!

00:21:13.390 --> 00:21:16.050
Will you let me borrow that deck?

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:20.070
I want to win with that deck.

00:21:22.450 --> 00:21:26.410
You said you were a professional 
duelist, so duel me.

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:32.460
Interesting.  You're saying that you 
can beat me with that lame deck?

00:21:32.460 --> 00:21:33.670
That's right.

00:21:34.050 --> 00:21:39.060
Of the numerous cards in existence, 
there is not a single useless card.

00:22:04.780 --> 00:22:10.360
What can we grasp?  What can we do?

00:22:10.720 --> 00:22:15.750
We'll step forward and find out

00:22:16.130 --> 00:22:21.680
My unstoppable emotions, the 
beating of my passionate heart

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:26.920
I heard the voice of truth

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:30.080
After I was hurt, I learned

00:22:32.650 --> 00:22:35.670
Of a place where I can become stronger

00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:42.830
I stack my dreams in my palm

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:48.230
And I'll someday pass them to you

00:22:48.660 --> 00:22:54.170
Seeking for the signal 
to start, my soul roars

00:22:54.470 --> 00:22:59.510
I will overcome my suffocating 
and mediocre life

00:23:00.070 --> 00:23:05.600
I'll dash and acquire all the bright futures

00:23:05.750 --> 00:23:15.020
Carrying the bonds I believe 
in, I run towards tomorrow
